src/test/prolly/README

The requirements suite
======================

These are tests of what the version-control engine must do, run against a
server: regression tests (sql/, listed in semantics_schedule), isolation
tests (specs/, listed in isolation_schedule) and TAP tests (t/).  Tests of
one interface or one implementation belong in src/test/modules/test_prolly
instead.

PROLLY_AM names the table access method the suite runs on, and
am/$(PROLLY_AM).conf holds the server settings that put new tables on it;
TAP tests get the same settings by making their servers with
ProllyTest::new_node.  Every group starts by checking that the settings are
in effect, so a mistake in them fails the run rather than letting the
suite test something else.

The tests of Postgres semantics expect exactly what stock Postgres does.
Running them on heap shows that the tests themselves are right:

    make -C src/test/prolly check       # every group, on PROLLY_AM
    make -C src/test/prolly check-heap  # the semantics groups, on heap

The groups can also be run one at a time: check-target, check-semantics,
check-isolation and check-tap-durability.  TAP tests are numbered by group:
0xx check that the access method under test is in effect, and 1xx check
durability.
